            <ArticleTitle>[Indications for enteroclysis. Retrospective study on 365 patients].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>332-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Small-bowel enema was performed in 536 patients referred for suspected malabsorption, enteritis, abdominal pain or obstruction. Lesions were found in 54% of cases. The positivity of the investigation was particularly high in clinically well-defined cases, such as suspected obstruction (80%) and enteritis (72%). The main indications and criteria of application of the investigation are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
